 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 531484,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "Students in a statistics class who were asked to provide their majors provided the data below:\n<table class=\"unnumbered\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Undecided</td>\n<td>Biology</td>\n<td>Biology</td>\n<td>Sociology</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Political Science</td>\n<td>Sociology</td>\n<td>Undecided</td>\n<td>Undecided</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Undecided</td>\n<td>Biology</td>\n<td>Biology</td>\n<td>Education</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Biology</td>\n<td>Biology</td>\n<td>Political Science</td>\n<td>Political Science</td>\n</tr></tbody>\n</table>",
   "stem_html": "Create a categorical frequency distribution to organize these responses.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>A categorical frequency distribution is a table with two columns. The first column contains all the categories present in the data, each listed once. The second column contains the frequencies of each category.</p>\n<p>Make a table with a header that describes your categories and labels for each row. The second column is labeled “Frequency.” Check your work by making sure the sum of the second column is correct.</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Major</th>\n<th>Frequency</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Biology</td>\n<td>6</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Education</td>\n<td>1</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Political science</td>\n<td>3</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Sociology</td>\n<td>2</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Undecided</td>\n<td>4</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Check the sum: 6 + 1 + 3 + 2 + 4 = 16</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<p>&nbsp;</p><table class=\"unnumbered\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Major</th>\n<th>Frequency</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Biology</td>\n<td>6</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Education</td>\n<td>1</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Political Science</td>\n<td>3</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Sociology</td>\n<td>2</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Undecided</td>\n<td>4</td>\n</tr></tbody>\n</table><p></p>\n"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
